SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Zone for Waydroid's bridge waydroid0; nazoos-welcome puts it here when
Waydroid is installed. Android gets DHCP and DNS from Waydroid's dnsmasq
on the host and reaches the internet via policy nazoos-waydroid-out, but
no other host service, because Android apps come from anywhere. Until
2026-10 the bridge was in "trusted", which accepts everything.
Doku: https://firewalld.org/documentation/man-pages/firewalld.zone.html
-->
<zone>
  <short>NazoOS Waydroid</short>
  <description>Android container (Waydroid): only DHCP and DNS reach this computer; connections to the internet and the local network are forwarded.</description>
  <service name="dhcp"/>
  <service name="dns"/>
</zone>
